  <data name="ToSMediaFull" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. GENERAL AGREEMENT
This application is a utility designed for displaying, playback, processing, and/or optimizing personal media files, including the backup and organization of digital content for personal use. By installing and using this software, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by these terms, specifically regarding the legal ownership of the media processed.

2. PERSONAL USE &amp; OWNERSHIP
This tool is intended solely for personal use and the management of legally owned digital content. Users must ensure they have the necessary rights, permissions, or legal ownership of any content processed through this application for the purpose of personal archiving or offline viewing. The conversion, modification, or processing of media files must not be used to create derivative works that infringe upon the original creator's moral or commercial rights. It must not be used to obtain, process, or distribute content in violation of any applicable laws.

3. COPYRIGHT &amp; DRM COMPLIANCE
Users are strictly prohibited from using this software to infringe upon any copyrights or intellectual property rights, or to circumvent digital rights management (DRM). The developer does not support, encourage, or facilitate unauthorized playback, reproduction, decryption, or unlocking of copyrighted material. This software is not intended for use with protected or encrypted streams.

4. FFMPEG &amp; TECHNICAL LIMITATIONS
For versions providing video or audio processing, this software utilizes the FFmpeg framework to perform playback, format conversion, and media handling. As an industry-standard technical tool, FFmpeg does not include functionality to bypass DRM systems or encrypted content protection. The developer shall not be liable for any inability to process protected content due to these inherent technical limitations.

5. NEUTRAL TECHNOLOGY PLATFORM
This software operates as a NEUTRAL TECHNOLOGY platform. It provides a technical interface and tools for users to access, organize, and manage content for personal consumption. By using this tool, you acknowledge that the software functions strictly as a conduit; the developer does not host, curate, provide, or exercise any editorial control over the content accessed by the user. The user is solely responsible for providing the sources or URLs and ensuring the legality of the accessed content.

6. THIRD-PARTY COMPLIANCE &amp; SERVICE DISRUPTION
By using this tool, you agree to comply with the Terms of Service and Community Guidelines of any third-party platforms you access. You acknowledge that:
- Third-Party Changes: Content providers may update their security protocols at any time. Such changes may cause temporary or permanent disruption of certain features.
- No Guarantee of Success: Due to geographic restrictions, server-side limitations, or technical changes by third parties, the developer does not guarantee that all content will be accessible at all times.
- As-Is Basis: This software is provided on an "As-Is" basis without commitment to a specific resolution timeframe for third-party disruptions.

7. REFUND POLICY &amp; FINALITY OF SALE
Your purchase (Premium/Pro/Plus) is for unlocking advanced technical features within the software interface. By purchasing, you acknowledge that:
- Third-Party Factors: Since disruptions or blocks caused by third-party platforms are beyond the developer's control, such interruptions do not constitute a software defect.
- Technical Limitations: Unintended software behaviors, bugs, or failure to process specific links due to geographic/server-side restrictions are not valid grounds for a refund request.
- Final Sale: This software is provided "As-Is." Once the premium features are activated, all sales are considered final.

8. USER RESPONSIBILITY &amp; LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
The developer shall NOT be held liable for any data loss, legal issues, or damages resulting from the use of this tool, including issues arising from software defects or coding errors. The user is solely responsible for maintaining independent backups of their original data before performing any conversion, transfer, or organization tasks. In any event, the developer's entire liability shall be limited strictly to the amount actually paid by you for the software.

9. NO AFFILIATION &amp; THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS
This application is an independent utility and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any third-party media platforms. All trademarks belong to their respective owners. Users must respect the intellectual property rights of creators and platforms at all times.

10. PRIVACY &amp; TECHNICAL DATA USAGE
This application is designed with a "Privacy-First" approach, operating primarily on a local basis.
- Local Processing: Core operations, including file handling and metadata processing, occur strictly on your local machine. No personally identifiable information (PII) or file content is ever collected or transmitted.
- Support &amp; Diagnosis: For the purpose of support and performance optimization, the application may collect non-personal technical data (OS version, CPU/GPU architecture, and anonymized crash logs).
- Execution Environment: We may collect anonymized technical metadata related to the application's runtime environment to ensure compatibility with our internal technical infrastructure.

11. MODIFICATIONS &amp; UPDATES
The developer reserves the right to update or modify these terms at any time without prior notice. Continued use of the software after any such modifications shall constitute your formal acceptance of the updated Terms of Service.</value>
